#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --script
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.11"
# dependencies = [
#     "httpx>=0.27",
# ]
# ///
"""emta — agent-first CLI for the Estonian Tax Board (maasikas.emta.ee).

This tool is designed to be invoked by agents. Run `emta help` to load the
full usage contract on demand — do not rely on memorised knowledge of its
surface. It is identity-free: it knows nothing about any consuming project's
person, company, or accounts.

AUTH MODEL — maasikas.emta.ee has TWO authenticated surfaces:

  (1) the PAS API — every URL under `/payments-and-settlements-api/`. Auth
      is a short-lived bearer (the `PAS-AUTHORIZATION` cookie, identical
      to the `Authorization: Bearer …` header) plus the `PAS-XSRF-TOKEN`
      and the cookie jar. THIS capability uses ONLY this surface. ONE
      paste of any PAS request unlocks every data verb: `balances`,
      `period-balances`, `interest`, `ledger`.
  (2) the customer-kmd2 Wicket app — the KMD declaration content (line
      values). A different, stateful session. This capability does NOT
      read it; declaration line values live on the books side.

  The customer-portal landing page and the `/customer-portal/access-token`
  request are the browser's internal login/bootstrap (they ride
  `JSESSIONID` and carry NO PAS bearer) — a paste of those is refused.

WHICH REQUEST TO COPY — unambiguous steps:

  1. Log in at maasikas.emta.ee with SmartID. You land on the
     customer-portal dashboard (it shows your prepayment account / tax
     obligations).
  2. Open devtools → Network. In the filter box type
     `payments-and-settlements-api`. Reload the page so the requests
     appear.
  3. Pick ANY listed request — an async XHR/fetch, NOT a
     document/navigation request — e.g. `session-user` or
     `prepay/account/active`. Right-click → Copy → Copy as cURL.
  4. Pipe it on stdin: `pbpaste | emta session ingest`.

  DO NOT copy: the `/customer-portal/...` page (document) request, the
  `access-token` request, or anything under `customer-kmd2/` — ingest
  refuses them (no PAS bearer / xsrf).

STARTUP PROTOCOL — stateful CLI, run this in order on the first call:

  1. `emta doctor`             — is a session stored and live?
  2. On `session_stale` (exit 2): paste a fresh PAS cURL (see WHICH
     REQUEST TO COPY above) via `emta session ingest`. Ingest stores the
     bearer + xsrf + cookie jar as per-connection state (mode 0600, never
     committed) and auto-discovers `principal_person_id` from a
     `/client/session-user` round-trip; the id is written to the ids store.
  3. Re-run `emta doctor` — it should report healthy.

SELF-HEAL
  - Any 401 or 406 on an authed call → exit 2 `session_stale`. The bearer
    is dead and there is nothing to refresh from — paste a fresh cURL.
  - There is no programmatic refresh: every authed call sends the stored
    bearer directly. ONE PAS paste unlocks every data verb until the
    bearer dies, then paste again.

SECRETS DISCIPLINE
  - The cURL paste enters through stdin only; argv is refused (argv leaks
    via process lists / shell history).
  - The stored bearer is a secret — same discipline as the cookies: lives
    in the state home (mode 0600), covered by the manager-owned
    `capabilities/.gitignore`, never logged, never printed, never committed.
  - `emta session show` prints only presence flags, cookie NAMES, and
    timestamps — never the bearer, the xsrf, or any cookie value.

IDENTIFIERS
  - `principal_person_id` — value sent as `x-principal-person-id` on every
    data call. AUTO-DISCOVERED by `emta session ingest` and `emta doctor`
    via a `/client/session-user` round-trip (the only authed call that
    needs no `x-principal-person-id`); written to the ids store. Override
    with `emta ids set principal_person_id <value>` if needed. The stored
    value is coerced to a string when sent — a numeric ids value works.

CONNECTIONS
  Configuration requires an explicit connections registry, even for one
  connection. Each connection keeps state under its id in project or user
  state. A
  project that drives several EMTA identities (e.g. several entities)
  declares them in `<project>/capabilities/emta/connections.json`:

    {
      "default": "<id>",
      "connections": {
        "<id>": { "allow_write": false }
      }
    }

  The registry resolves project envelope first, else the machine-level
  ~/.config/emta/connections.json; first found wins, never merged. Sessions
  are kept per connection in the state home, so two connections never share
  a session. EMTA exposes no env-resolvable secret — the cascade has nothing
  to resolve (see deviations.md) — so a connection entry carries no
  `secret_env`. `allow_write` is accepted, but the surface is read-only, so
  no verb is gated by it.

  Selection: `--connection <id>` accepted anywhere on the line.

COMMANDS

  emta help                                  this contract
  emta doctor [--connection <id>]            probe with stored creds via
                                             /client/session-user; refresh
                                             principal_person_id on 200
  emta session ingest                        read a `Copy as cURL` on
                                             stdin; persist bearer + xsrf
                                             + cookies to per-connection
                                             state; bootstrap via
                                             session-user; auto-set
                                             principal_person_id
  emta session show [--connection <id>]      masked summary: bearer/xsrf
                                             present, cookie names,
                                             ingested-at; never values
  emta session clear [--connection <id>]     drop per-connection state
  emta balances [--connection <id>]          current prepay account balances
  emta period-balances --date YYYY-MM-DD     per-tax-period balances on a
                  [--connection <id>]        date; rows de-duplicated on
                                             (taxPeriodCode, claimTypeCode,
                                             documentNr)
  emta interest --date YYYY-MM-DD            per-tax-period interest on a
                  [--connection <id>]        date (sibling of
                                             period-balances; chases
                                             interest / cent gaps); rows
                                             de-duplicated on the same key
  emta ledger --from YYYY-MM-DD              prepay ledger movements;
              --to YYYY-MM-DD                EMTA refuses multi-year spans
              [--connection <id>]            — --from and --to must be in
                                             the same calendar year

CONTRACT COMMANDS (the same on every capability):
  emta connections                           where every connection's
                                             values resolve from; secrets
                                             masked; local only
  emta stub                                  one-line awareness text
  emta manifest --json                       machine-readable declaration
  emta guide [<topic>]                       guide topics / one guide body
                                             (none ship initially)
  emta ids list|get <l>|set <l> <v>|rm <l>   project identifiers envelope
        [--note <text>]                      (capabilities/emta/identifiers.json)
  emta refs                                  menu of the project's reference
                                             files for this capability

EXIT CODES
  0  success
  2  auth / session_stale — paste a fresh cURL via `emta session ingest`
  3  not found — unknown identifier, missing guide topic, etc.
  4  policy refusal — the project gate, or a write verb on a read-only
     connection (this CLI is read-only, no verb is gated)
  5  network / server — timeout, 5xx, transport error
  6  input / validation — bad date, multi-year ledger span, malformed cURL
"""

